WEBVTT

NOTE Draft cue timing follows measured scene audio and word count. Review spoken word alignment before publication.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.038
Welcome to Resgrid Academy. In this lesson, we will match subscription capacity to

00:00:05.038 --> 00:00:10.075
the roster. Large onboarding can stop at personnel or unit limits when capacity

00:00:10.075 --> 00:00:15.112
has not been reviewed in advance. We will explain the features, the setup

00:00:15.112 --> 00:00:18.600
decisions, and a practical way to check the result.

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:24.166
Before inviting 40 new members, an administrator confirms the plan has room or

00:00:24.166 --> 00:00:29.133
asks the managing member to change it. Adding members or units stops at

00:00:29.133 --> 00:00:34.099
the plan limit, so check the remaining room before a large onboarding. The

00:00:34.099 --> 00:00:39.066
examples in this series use a fictional department and are teaching scenarios, not

00:00:39.066 --> 00:00:39.830
default settings.

00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:45.668
Base plans and capacity. Your plan, its personnel and unit limits, and your

00:00:45.668 --> 00:00:50.100
add-ons. Check the remaining room before adding many members or units.

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:57.056
For the training scenario, work in this order. Step 1. Review the observed

00:00:57.056 --> 00:01:03.413
base plan, personnel count, and unit count. Step 2. Compare planned onboarding with

00:01:03.413 --> 00:01:09.280
available capacity. Step 3. Review add-on entitlements and their separate configuration prerequisites.

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:15.708
Now verify the result. Check observed subscription evidence and current resource counts. Use

00:01:15.708 --> 00:01:21.537
the owning billing screen for any authorized subscription change. A common problem to

00:01:21.537 --> 00:01:27.365
watch for: Missing billing evidence means capacity is unknown. Only the managing member

00:01:27.365 --> 00:01:28.710
performs subscription changes.

00:01:29.310 --> 00:01:34.683
Your practice task is simple. Compare current counts with a proposed roster expansion.

00:01:34.683 --> 00:01:40.057
Document headroom and optional add-ons without purchasing anything. Record the result, who owns

00:01:40.057 --> 00:01:45.430
the follow-up, and when it should be reviewed. Use the linked feature scripts

00:01:45.430 --> 00:01:47.910
for the detailed screen recording plan.

